19. The "first point of divergence" concept

I want to emphasize this because it will make your analysis much more sophisticated.

Suppose you have:

EFFECTIVE-DATE

COBOL
Input = 01/01
   ↓
Intermediate = 01/01
   ↓
Condition A = TRUE
   ↓
Output = 01/01


SQL
Input = 01/01
   ↓
Intermediate = 01/01
   ↓
Condition A equivalent = TRUE
   ↓
Output = 01/08

The problem isn't the input.

The problem is downstream.

But imagine:

COBOL:
Input = 01/01
   ↓
Intermediate = 01/01

SQL:
Input = 01/01
   ↓
Intermediate = 01/08

Then you know the problem occurs before that intermediate value.

Your final report should identify:

> First point of divergence: SQL date derivation.



That's much more actionable for the .NET team.


