24. Your evidence standard

I'd establish this rule at the very beginning:

🟢 Confirmed

Directly supported by source.

Example:

> AMC20W moves field A to field B under condition C.



🟡 Inferred

Strongly suggested but not explicitly established.

Example:

> Field A appears to represent the previous managed-care value based on how it is maintained across records.



🔴 Unresolved

The available artifacts aren't enough.

Example:

> The SQL implementation appears to use the most recent effective date, but available source does not establish whether COBOL's "previous" record is defined by effective date or physical file sequence.



This distinction will protect you when you present the work.


