One final recommendation

Because you have the functional specs for AMC05W/10W/15W/20W/25W/30W/AMCMRG, don't restrict Copilot's investigation only to the four programs in the stated flow.

Those additional programs may contain upstream logic or business rules that explain why a field has a particular value before it reaches AMC10W/20W/30W.

So your rule should be:

> Start with AMCMRG → AMC10W → AMC20W → AMC30W, but follow every dependency that can influence one of the seven fields, even if it takes you into AMC05W, AMC15W, AMC25W, another copybook, or another called program.



That is how I'd make this a forensic reconciliation rather than a superficial code comparison.

And importantly, if after all of this you conclude "we cannot prove the root cause without actual input/output data", that is a valid and professional conclusion. You can still give the team the exact three or four hypotheses and the regression cases needed to prove which one is responsible.
